From: thororen <78185467+thororen1234@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:43:05 -0400
Subject: build: use the Rust std Windows 7 code paths

Rust's std imports Windows 8+ functions (GetSystemTimePreciseAsFileTime,
WaitOnAddress, ...) unless it's built for a *-win7-windows-msvc target.
Since Chromium builds std from source, enable its target_vendor="win7"
code paths on Windows x86 and x64.

This patch is needed for Windows 7 support and is not suitable for
upstreaming.

diff --git a/build/rust/std/rules/BUILD.gn b/build/rust/std/rules/BUILD.gn
index e1fe3a334079b1be5825e38ac7993030e9670b41..597eda7f72e8122813702ed46f447806ee61762d 100644
--- a/build/rust/std/rules/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/rust/std/rules/BUILD.gn
@@ -3261,6 +3261,14 @@ cargo_crate("std") {
     "-Zforce-unstable-if-unmarked",
     "--cap-lints=allow",  # Suppress all warnings in stdlib crates
   ]
+  if (is_win && current_cpu != "arm64") {
+    # Electron: use std's Windows 7 code paths, as the *-win7-windows-msvc
+    # targets do, so that it doesn't import Windows 8+ functions.
+    rustflags += [
+      "--cfg=target_vendor=\"win7\"",
+      "-Aexplicit_builtin_cfgs_in_flags",
+    ]
+  }
   output_dir =
       "$root_out_dir/local_rustc_sysroot/lib/rustlib/$rust_abi_target/lib/"
 }
